WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.944
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.244 --> 00:00:08.514
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.814 --> 00:00:15.472
Unit twenty-one: Healthy Screen Habits. Today you will talk about screen time with too much and too many.

4
00:00:15.772 --> 00:00:18.598
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:22.789
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.034
Screen time.

7
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:30.105
Screen time means time spent looking at phones, TVs and computers.

8
00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:32.751
I try to limit my screen time.

9
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.281
Your turn. Say: Screen time.

10
00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:40.285
Screen time.

11
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:41.738
Phone.

12
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:46.294
Phone means a small device to call, text and use apps.

13
00:00:46.883 --> 00:00:48.651
I put my phone away at dinner.

14
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.380
Your turn. Say: Phone.

15
00:00:54.233 --> 00:00:55.049
Phone.

16
00:00:55.783 --> 00:00:56.726
Sleep.

17
00:00:57.717 --> 00:01:00.575
Sleep means rest when your eyes are closed at night.

18
00:01:01.183 --> 00:01:03.427
Teenagers need nine hours of sleep.

19
00:01:04.017 --> 00:01:06.402
Your turn. Say: Sleep.

20
00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:10.186
Sleep.

21
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:11.823
Eyes.

22
00:01:12.817 --> 00:01:15.246
Eyes means the parts of your body you see with.

23
00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:17.803
Bright screens can hurt your eyes.

24
00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:20.686
Your turn. Say: Eyes.

25
00:01:23.533 --> 00:01:24.592
Eyes.

26
00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:26.084
Break.

27
00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:28.758
Break means a short rest.

28
00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.175
Take a break every hour.

29
00:01:31.783 --> 00:01:34.238
Your turn. Say: Break.

30
00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:37.764
Break.

31
00:01:38.517 --> 00:01:39.390
Balance.

32
00:01:40.383 --> 00:01:42.894
Balance means the right amount of different things.

33
00:01:43.483 --> 00:01:46.156
I keep a balance between study and games.

34
00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.240
Your turn. Say: Balance.

35
00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.066
Balance.

36
00:01:53.817 --> 00:01:54.609
Limit.

37
00:01:55.617 --> 00:01:57.860
Limit means the most that is allowed.

38
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.345
My limit is two hours a day.

39
00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.463
Your turn. Say: Limit.

40
00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.185
Limit.

41
00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:08.951
Offline.

42
00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.217
Offline means not using the internet.

43
00:02:12.817 --> 00:02:15.083
I spend Sunday afternoon offline.

44
00:02:15.683 --> 00:02:18.069
Your turn. Say: Offline.

45
00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:22.074
Offline.

46
00:02:22.867 --> 00:02:26.552
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.417 --> 00:02:30.891
Visal, how much screen time do you have each day?

48
00:02:31.983 --> 00:02:34.903
About five hours. Is that too much?

49
00:02:36.017 --> 00:02:38.669
Yes, it's too much. How do you feel?

50
00:02:39.783 --> 00:02:42.526
My eyes hurt, and I don't get enough sleep.

51
00:02:43.617 --> 00:02:46.417
Try setting a limit and taking breaks.

52
00:02:47.517 --> 00:02:52.514
Good idea. I'll also stop opening too many apps at night.

53
00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:55.225
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:56.083 --> 00:02:58.652
Grammar focus: Too much and too many.

55
00:02:58.952 --> 00:03:00.150
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.035
Too much screen time is unhealthy.

57
00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.833
I have too many apps on my phone.

58
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.469
Too much light at night hurts your sleep.

59
00:03:10.433 --> 00:03:15.710
Use 'too much' with things you can't count (time, water). Use 'too many' with plural nouns (apps, games).

60
00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:20.321
Be careful! Don't say: Too many screen time is unhealthy.

61
00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:25.091
Say: Too much screen time is unhealthy.

62
00:03:25.391 --> 00:03:28.075
Use 'too much' with uncountable nouns like time.

63
00:03:28.867 --> 00:03:31.380
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:33.528
Finding a Balance.

65
00:03:33.828 --> 00:03:36.779
Too much screen time can hurt your eyes and your sleep.

66
00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:41.612
Too many notifications also break your concentration.

67
00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.039
Set a limit on your phone, and take a break every hour.

68
00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:49.660
Spend time offline with your family and friends.

69
00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:53.177
A healthy balance helps your body and your mind.

70
00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:58.326
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:59.183 --> 00:04:01.578
blank screen time is bad for you.

72
00:04:01.878 --> 00:04:04.985
A, Too much. B, Too many. C, Too.

73
00:04:08.533 --> 00:04:10.417
The answer is A: Too much.

74
00:04:11.583 --> 00:04:13.327
A short rest is a blank.

75
00:04:13.627 --> 00:04:16.782
A, break. B, limit. C, balance.

76
00:04:20.333 --> 00:04:22.066
The answer is A: break.

77
00:04:23.217 --> 00:04:25.089
Not using the internet is blank.

78
00:04:25.389 --> 00:04:29.460
A, offline. B, online. C, on screen.

79
00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.976
The answer is A: offline.

80
00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:39.620
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:40.483 --> 00:04:42.738
How much screen time is healthy for you?

82
00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:52.957
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:53.257 --> 00:05:01.541
I think two hours a day is healthy for me. Too much screen time makes me tired, so I go offline after nine o'clock.

84
00:05:01.841 --> 00:05:03.527
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:04.417 --> 00:05:08.404
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and too much and too many.

86
00:05:08.704 --> 00:05:14.073
Today's value is self-discipline. Control your habits, so your habits do not control you.

87
00:05:14.373 --> 00:05:17.176
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

88
00:05:17.476 --> 00:05:20.013
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

